1. d4 d5 2. c4 c6 { The Slav: supporting d5 with the c-pawn keeps the c8 bishop free. }
3. Nf3 { [%name Main line, Dutch Variation] }
( 3. cxd5 { [%name Exchange Variation] A symmetrical structure; Black simply copies and develops. }
  3... cxd5 4. Nc3 Nf6 5. Bf4 Nc6 6. e3 Bf5 7. Nf3 e6 { Equal and solid; Black's pieces are just as active as White's. } )
3... Nf6 4. Nc3
( 4. e3 { [%name 4.e3] White protects c4 but locks in the c1 bishop. }
  4... Bf5 5. Nc3 e6 6. Nh4 { Chasing the bishop to win the bishop pair. }
  6... Bg6 7. Nxg6 hxg6 8. Bd3 Nbd7 9. O-O Bd6 { The h-file is half-open for Black's rook as compensation. } )
4... dxc4 { Taking the pawn while White's c4 is unprotected. }
5. a4 Bf5 { The bishop gets out before ...e6; a4 stopped ...b5. }
6. e3 e6 7. Bxc4 Bb4 8. O-O Nbd7 9. Qe2 Bg6 10. e4 O-O 11. e5 Nd5 { The knight lands on the strong d5 square; Black is solid and active. } *
